{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"Stable React releases follow semantic versioning (semver) principles.","source_span":"Stable React releases (also known as \"Latest\" release channel) follow [semantic versioning (semver)]"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"Critical bug fixes are released as patch releases, changing the z number, e.g. 15.6.2 to 15.6.3.","source_span":"When releasing **critical bug fixes**, we make a **patch release** by changing the **z** number (ex: 15.6.2 to 15.6.3)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"New features or non-critical fixes are released as minor releases, changing the y number, e.g. 15.6.2 to 15.7.0.","source_span":"When releasing **new features** or **non-critical fixes**, we make a **minor release** by changing the **y** number (ex: 15.6.2 to 15.7.0)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"Breaking changes are released as major releases, changing the x number, e.g. 15.6.2 to 16.0.0.","source_span":"When releasing **breaking changes**, we make a **major release** by changing the **x** number (ex: 15.6.2 to 16.0.0)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"React 15 was released in April 2016.","source_span":"React 15 was released in April 2016"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"React 16 was released in September 2017.","source_span":"React 16 was released in September 2017"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"React 17 was released in October 2020.","source_span":"React 17 was released in October 2020"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"The Facebook codebase alone has over 50,000 React components.","source_span":"The Facebook codebase alone has over 50,000 React components."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"Facebook tests upgrade paths using a team of less than 10 people to update the 50,000+ React components.","source_span":"if our team of less than 10 people can update 50,000+ components alone"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"Changes to APIs starting with unstable_ don't count as breaking changes requiring a major version bump.","source_span":"**APIs starting with `unstable_`.** These are provided as experimental features whose APIs we are not yet confident in."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"Development warnings don't affect the runtime behavior of an app, and production builds don't log them.","source_span":"Development warnings won't affect the runtime behavior of your app... the production build won't log the warnings"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","statement":"If a security vulnerability is found in React, a backported fix is released for all major versions affected by the vulnerability.","source_span":"If we learn of a security vulnerability in React, we release a backported fix for all major versions that are affected by the vulnerability."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What version-number change signals a \"patch\" release in React's versioning policy, and what's an example?","answer":"The z number changes (e.g. 15.6.2 to 15.6.3); patch releases are reserved for critical bug fixes."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","fact_refs":[4,5,6],"question":"When were React 15, React 16, and React 17 released?","answer":"React 15 was released in April 2016, React 16 in September 2017, and React 17 in October 2020."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","fact_refs":[7],"question":"How many React components does the Facebook codebase contain, according to the versioning policy page?","answer":"Over 50,000 React components."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","fact_refs":[9],"question":"Does changing an API prefixed with unstable_ count as a breaking change requiring a major version bump?","answer":"No — APIs starting with unstable_ are experimental and changes to them are not counted as breaking changes."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_versioning-policy","fact_refs":[11],"question":"What does React do if a security vulnerability is discovered that affects older major versions still used in production?","answer":"React releases a backported fix for all major versions affected by the vulnerability."}
